  faqs={[
    { q: 'How long can a student realistically focus?', a: 'Most people do 25 to 50 minutes of genuine focus before attention dips. That is normal. The goal is not one long unbroken stretch but several good blocks with real breaks between them.' },
    { q: 'Does music help you focus while studying?', a: 'Lyrics compete with reading and tend to hurt comprehension. Instrumental or ambient sound can help mask a noisy room. If a task is hard, silence usually wins.' },
